{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And one who steals.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said: Why does this verse come between one who strikes his father and one who curses his father? He answered that the verse speaks only of what typically happens, for those stolen were young, and they grew up in a foreign land and do not know their fathers, and it is possible that they strike them and curse them, and the punishment falls upon the thief." "Or if he is found in his hand in the market before he has sold him, he shall be put to death."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:55.097896859Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}